## 8️⃣ Backend Contract (Actual)

There is no REST endpoint at `/ai/explain-score` — the frontend calls the Supabase edge function directly via the SDK, from `src/lib/aiExplainer.ts`:

```ts
supabase.functions.invoke("explain-fit", { body: { ...scoreResult fields } })
```

Payload fields sent (flattened, not nested under `scoreResult`): `supplierName`, `buyerName`, `corridor`, `status`, `totalScore`, `readinessScore`, `passedHardGates`, `hardGateFailures`, `readinessBreakdown`, `riskPenalties`, `gaps`.

Response:

```json
{
  "explanation": "..."
}
```

If the edge function call fails → `explainFitWithAI()` catches the error and returns `null`, and the UI treats that as "no explanation available." This matches the spirit of the original doc even though the transport mechanism differs.

